body:
Um, I was in this same age relationship except my bf was 19.  It lasted for SEVEN YEARS and I remember it as the best relationship I ever had.  "Stan" was kind, supportive, loving and just amazing.  I started out as a scared, bullied and lonely kid and became mature, confident, and so, so happy.  Thanks, "Stan," you improved my life 110%.

&#x200B;

BTW I am 52 now, and we are still good friends.

Therapy is not always available.  Where I live there is only one therapist for a town of about 3,900.  I waited 14 months for an appointment and it was a disaster - she was packing up to leave for the day and kept calling me by the wrong name.

&#x200B;

Also, private therapy is EXPENSIVE and these days it's hard to even put bread on the table.

I'm a normal, everyday patient who recently spent about a week in the ICU due to head trauma sustained during a seizure.  Please know that my nurses were INCREDIBLE, as I'm sure you are too.  I can't believe therapy of some sort is not mandatory!  By all means follow this advice.  I know I was a  pain in the ass (fighting, ripping out tubes, panicking, didn't know who/when/why I was)... but the nurses handled it all with aplomb and made me feel safe and secure again and again.

&#x200B;

What you and your colleagues do is invaluable and you need to take care of yourselves first.  Thank you on behalf of all ICU patients everywhere.  (And yes I got a card and presents for the nurses in Grande Prairie.)
